  "task": {
    "objective": "Serve two hot courses and two chilled desserts using three trays, six total ingredients, two portable ice boxes and a finite cooling/fuel reserve.",
    "natural_termination": "Success when both served counts reach two. Failure when remaining pantry stock plus raw/processing/ready portions of either type cannot supply that type's remaining demand. Spoiled food is irrecoverable.",
    "interaction": "A moved box changes both walkability and nearby tray temperatures; it can preserve a peer dessert but chill another peer hot course. Door access spends shared cooling, while cooling/refill/processing/washing and one shared corridor couple the cooks' schedules.",
    "observation_access": "Fully observable. The flat public obs_keys vector includes every cook/item position, carrier, type, food, processing state, temperature, freshness, clock, portable charge, map, door state, cooling/fuel store, station, ingredient and service counter, and per-step event. The chilled flag reports cooling actually applied on the just-finished step, not a promise of cooling after reserves deplete. All active entities are visible to all roles; human and policy information is identical."
  },
